AB  - Increasing the importance of sustainable agriculture makes calculating water footprint necessary to understand environmental impacts due to agricultural products. However, it is boring while it prone to errors. In the current research work, an issue of correct estimation of water footprints was approached directly with digital technologies of machine learning, deep learning, and geographic information systems (GIS). We use advanced algorithms, such as Vision transformer and Temporary Fusion Transformer algorithms to analyze satellite imagery, soil moisture data, and weather patterns to estimate the water footprints of different agricultural products. This approach enables farmers, policymakers, and other stakeholders to make accurate and efficient calculations of water footprints in decision-making for water management and sustainable agriculture practices. The outcome of this research demonstrates the potential of digital technologies in promoting sustainable agriculture and reducing the environmental impact of agricultural production.  © 2025 IEEE.
