AU  - Pius, A.A.; Sino, R.M.; James, D.; Santhosh, E.; Rohith, M.P.
TI  - Sustania: A Digital Farming Ecosystem for Smart Agriculture
T2  - Proceedings of the ACCTHPA 2025 - Conference on 2025 Advanced Computing and Communication Technologies for High Performance Applications
LA  - English
KW  - agricultural technology; climate change; IoT integration; irrigation system; machine learning; precision agriculture; remote sensing; sustainable agriculture; water conservation; Agricultural machinery; Ecosystems; Internet of things; Irrigation; Learning algorithms; Learning systems; Machine learning; Precision agriculture; Smart agriculture; Soil moisture; Soil temperature; Soil testing; Sustainable agriculture; Temperature sensors; %moisture; Agricultural technologies; Internet of thing integration; Irrigation systems; Machine-learning; Precision Agriculture; Random forest classifier; Remote-sensing; Smart agricultures; Sustainable agriculture; Remote sensing; Water conservation
AB  - We have developed an innovative Smart Irrigation System to address recent challenges in agricultural water management and to meet the growing need for sustainable farming practices, particularly for small- and medium-scale farmers. The system integrates Internet of Things (IoT)-based sensors, machine learning algorithms, and a user-friendly web interface to optimize water usage in agricultural settings. It uses soil moisture and temperature sensors along with a Random Forest classifier, ensuring precise and reliable scheduling. The platform features a modular architecture with an SQLite backend and a React-based front-end, making it a cost-effective solution. Initial testing was conducted using a DHT11 temperature sensor and a resistive soil moisture sensor; however, subsequent evaluations demonstrated that the DHT22 temperature sensor provided better performance and durability. After extensive comparison, the Random Forest classifier was selected for model training, as it proved to be the fastest and most accurate option with an accuracy of 91 %. Core features of the system include real-time temperature and moisture updates and predictive capabilities based on these readings. Our system has been named 'Sustania' due to its potential to serve as a valuable tool for farmers transitioning to the modern era of sustainable and innovative farming. © 2025 IEEE.
