TI  - IoT Enabled Smart Irrigation IR based Field Security and Cloud Integrated Data Management for Sustainable Agriculture
T2  - Proceedings of 4th International Conference on Electronics and Renewable Systems, ICEARS 2026
LA  - English
KW  - DHT11 Sensor; GSM Module; Soil Moisture Sensor; USB Web CAM; Global system for mobile communications; Hydration; Infrared detectors; Internet of things; Irrigation; Remote sensing; Smart agriculture; Sustainable development; Agriculture systems; DHT11 sensor; Environmental fields; Environmental Monitoring; GSM module; Integrated data management; Security features; Soil moisture sensors; Sustainable agriculture; USB web CAM; Soil moisture
AB  - This project presents an IoT-based intelligent agriculture system built on a Raspberry Pi platform. The setup integrates automated irrigation, environmental monitoring, and field security features. Soil moisture sensors continuously track soil hydration, and when levels fall below a set threshold, a relay-operated water pump is triggered to provide efficient irrigation. Temperature and humidity are monitored using a DHT11 sensor, supplying essential environmental data to support optimal plant growth. For enhanced farm security, an infrared sensor and USB camera detect movement from intruders or animals, triggering an alarm and sending instant alerts to the farmer via GSM. By combining automation, sensing, and security, the proposed system reduces manual labor, conserves water, and protects crops - offering a reliable and scalable solution for sustainable smart farming. © 2026 IEEE.
