KW  - AI in Crop Health Monitoring; Convolutional Neural Networks; Plant Disease Detection; Precision Agriculture. Geospatial Analytics. Remote Sensing in Agriculture; Crops; Diagnosis; Diseases; Ecosystems; Maps; Neural networks; Plant diseases; Plants (botany); Precision agriculture; Smart agriculture; Soil testing; AI in crop health monitoring; Convolutional neural network; Disease detection; Geo-spatial; Geospatial analytic.; Health monitoring; Plant disease; Plant disease detection; Precision Agriculture; Precision agriculture.; Remote sensing in agriculture; Remote-sensing; Remote sensing
AB  - Fast and accurate plant disease detection is essential for agricultural production and ecologically sustainable farming. The research paper defines GACN, a Geospatial data and AI-powered Crop disease detection Network. GACN uses spatial data analytics and CNNs to diagnose plant diseases more accurately, improving farming. The latest GACN development utilizes a curated dataset of over 50,000 annotated leaf photos. This collection covers fifteen crop kinds and twenty-five illnesses across many agroclimatic zones. GACN's F1-score is 95.2 %, recall 94.9 %, precision 95.5%, and classification accuracy 96.8%. Because of this, it can consistently locate ill individuals in the real world. The GACN develops disease risk maps that predict disease locations with an accuracy of over 92 %, using weather patterns, soil moisture data, and satellite-derived vegetation indicators (NDVI and LST). This multimodal technique enables early illness identification and localization prediction. Agronomists and farmers can use the system's decision support platform on their mobile devices for real-time warnings, regional treatment recommendations, and interactive maps and visualizations. Three Kenyan and Indian testing locations show the model's scalability and endurance. Additionally, it could cut crop losses by 38 %. The GACN has built data-driven, strong agricultural ecosystems using AI and geospatial intelligence. © 2025 IEEE.
