AU  - Korav, S.; Singh, U.K.
TI  - Water Conservation and AI
T2  - Handbook of Digitalization and Big Data in the Water Sector: International Case Studies: (Volume 3
LA  - English
KW  - Agricultural machinery; Learning algorithms; Learning systems; Precision agriculture; Water conservation; Water management; Water quality; Artificial intelligence technologies; Early Warning System; Intelligence models; Latest development; Living organisms; Management strategies; Precision-farming; Water management approaches; Water networks; Waters resources; Artificial intelligence
AB  - Water is an essential resource for all living organisms on Earth, but its accessibility is becoming more restricted. This study explores how artificial intelligence (AI) could help tackle the urgent challenges of water conservation, emphasizing the administration and allocation of water, precision farming, assessing water quality, weather forecasting and developing early warning systems, and the model of intelligent water networks. Hence, it is vital to adopt advanced management strategies for water resources. This chapter explores how AI contributes to water conservation by examining various water management approaches. It offers an in-depth look at the latest developments in AI modelling concerning water-related factors, such as rainfall run-off, evaporation, evapotranspiration, water quality indicators, streamflow, sediment transport, and the variations in dam or lake levels. The discussion underscores the significance of enhancing water resource management in precision agriculture, demonstrating how AI technologies can greatly boost water use efficiency in farming practices. By integrating tools like remote sensing and machine learning algorithms with vital elements such as soil moisture monitoring, crop health evaluation, and water requirement analysis, farmers gain access to data-driven insights that help them make informed decisions about irrigation. The focus of this chapter is on the prospective evolution of water conservation methodologies through the application of AI technologies. It highlights the significance of water quality monitoring, and the implementation of early warning systems as proactive measures for effective water management in the face of future challenges. © 2026 selection and editorial matter, Tonni Agustiono Kurniawan and Abdelkader Anouzla; individual chapters, the contributors.
