KW  - Digital Transformation of Agriculture; Dynamic Monitoring of Farmland Environment; Integration of Artificial Intelligence Technology; Smart Agriculture; Ultra-Long-Distance Dual-Rotating Laser; Agricultural economics; Digital devices; Digital integrated circuits; Farms; Remote sensing; Rotation; Smart agriculture; Soil surveys; Soil temperature; Artificial intelligence technologies; Digital transformation; Digital transformation of agriculture; Dynamic monitoring; Dynamic monitoring of farmland environment; Integration of artificial intelligence technology; Laser detection; Smart agricultures; Ultra longs; Ultra-long-distance dual-rotating laser; Soil moisture
AB  - Aiming at the bottleneck of limited coverage and insufficient real-time performance of traditional agricultural monitoring technology, a dynamic monitoring system based on the fusion of ultra-long-range dual-rotation laser detection and artificial intelligence is proposed. The system realizes sub-meter resolution scanning of soil moisture, temperature, nutrients and other farmland environmental parameters within a radius of 5 km through a dual-band laser device, optimizes the communication efficiency by combining the 5G edge node with LoRa hybrid networking, constructs a lightweight CNN-LSTM hybrid model, realizes the dynamic fusion of multi-source data, and achieves an inference speed of 43 ms/frame at the edge end. The experimental results show that: the laser detection coverage rate reaches 98.2%, the soil moisture and temperature detection error is controlled within 2.4% and 0.5°C, respectively; the prediction accuracy of the AI model is improved by 12.7% under multi-source data fusion (F1-score=0.92), the system deployment cost is reduced by 40% compared with the traditional solution of 250,000 yuan/thousand acres, and the payback period is shortened to 3 years (ROI=133%). 133%). The study provides a ground-level technology complement to the sky-ground integrated agricultural remote sensing network with both ecological and economic benefits. © 2025 Published by SPIE.
