TI  - Revolutionizing agriculture by advanced water and irrigation management technologies
T2  - Emerging Trends and Technologies in Water Management and Conservation
LA  - English
KW  - Agribusiness; Climate change; Crops; Data integration; Soil moisture; Sprinkler systems (irrigation); Subirrigation; Water management; Drip irrigation; Irrigation management; Irrigation methods; Labor costs; Management technologies; Positive changes; Sprinkler irrigation; Surface irrigation; Water scarcity; Waters managements; Wages
AB  - Developments in water and irrigation technologies for agriculture are an incredible shift towards positive change in productivity while addressing water issues. The conventional irrigation methods under consideration are the surface, sprinkler and drip irrigation and as pointed out earlier these are grievously deficient in terms of parameters such as water wastage and increased labor costs. It then addresses smart technologies in irrigation such as soil moisture sensor, weather-based controller, precisions irrigation system, and remote sensing. These allow specific water application for crops and effective use of water since application is based on crop requirement or weather condition. By adapting measures such as deficit irrigation, waste water recycling, rainwater harvesting, and the use of crops that resist water stress are also presented as measures to cope with water shortage. It shows clear examples of applications of these technologies that have saved water and boosted yields in agriculture around the world. However, there are challenges that exist these include data integration, high cost for its implementation to act as a barrier to access, energy dependence, and lack of familiarity among farmers. The challenges set for the future include defining the universality of the data models, inventing cheap solutions, incorporating the use of renewable energy, innovating interfaces and educating farmers more properly. With climate change bringing the already difficult water resources management in agriculture into a new level of challenge through exacerbation of water scarcity, there is need for adoption of advanced technologies and installation of new policies as well as strict implementation of sustainable practices. These technologies present some highly effective methods for managing and providing water for irrigational purposes as the world faces a challenge of water scarcity. © 2025, IGI Global Scientific Publishing. All rights reserved.
