AB  - Real-time monitoring of crops with the help of technology can monitor and regulate environmental and crop conditions. The SmartCorp Monitoring System will be a development of an advanced environment control system for corporate agriculture through the NodeMCU ESP8266 microcontroller. It would possess moisture sensors that automatically trigger a water pump when the measured moisture is lower than the threshold and PIR motion sensors to automatically monitor human presence as a means of upgrading security. The system, with the inclusion of Wi-Fi, gives users real-time control from a distance by accessing a web interface or a mobile application. It is powered by a 18650 battery to provide enough energy, ensuring that wherever it is located, the area is limited to electricity. Manual control is also made possible through a tactile pushbutton, and at the same time, it is flexible.The system minimizes the low efficiency of water distribution during irrigation while saving it, by securing the farm, through simplified operations. © 2025 IEEE.
