KW  - Frequency Modulated Continuous Wave Radar (FMCW); GNU Radio; Software Defined Radio (SDR); USRP; Agriculture; Application programs; Continuous wave radar; Cost effectiveness; Frequency estimation; Radar measurement; Radar signal processing; Radio; Remote sensing; Software radio; Soil moisture; Soil surveys; Water management; Cost effective; Frequency modulated continuous wave radar; Frequency-modulated-continuous-wave radars; GNU radio; Primary objective; Radar technology; Software defined radio; Software-defined radios; Soil moisture estimation; USRP; Frequency modulation
AB  - This study explores the application of Frequency Modulated Continuous Wave (FMCW) radar technology utilizing Software Defined Radio (SDR) and GNU Radio for the feasibility of soil moisture estimation. The primary objective is to develop a cost-effective radar system capable of real-time monitoring of soil moisture content in agricultural settings. The methodology involves designing an FMCW radar operating and processing the acquired signals through GNU Radio to extract dielectric properties of the soil. Key findings indicate that the FMCW radar can effectively measure soil moisture, although vegetation interference poses challenges to accuracy. The implications of this research highlight the potential of FMCW radar technology for enhancing agricultural practices and optimizing water resource management, paving the way for future advancements in remote sensing applications for soil moisture monitoring and mapping. © 2024 IEEE.
